+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a financially solid quarter, with revenue of $720,000 against total spend of $464,000, producing an operating surplus of $256,000. Support held a high close rate on a growing ticket volume, and the security team resolved the large majority of detected incidents. The delivery team's new project kicked off in October, with a launch expected in the second half of the month. Several figures published in the source packets' own summaries did not match the underlying line-item data and have been recalculated below; see Notes for detail.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+- **Finance spend discrepancy:** the finance packet's stated total spend ($463,250) does not match the sum of its own line items (Payroll $286,400 + Infrastructure $81,750 + Contractors $64,200 + Facilities $31,650 = $464,000, a $750 gap). The recalculated total ($464,000) is used above for spend and operating surplus; finance should confirm which figure is authoritative.
+- **Support close rate discrepancy:** the support packet's headline close rate (96.4%) does not match its own ticket counts (1,171 closed / 1,250 opened = 93.7%). The recalculated rate is used above; recommend the support dashboard's calculation be audited.
+- **Delivery launch date discrepancy:** the delivery packet's stated launch date (2026-10-22) does not match the plan when phase durations (Discovery 3, Build 6, QA 4, Release 1 business days, sequential, next phase starting the next business day) are applied against the 2026-10-05 start date and the 2026-10-12 company holiday. Recomputing the schedule yields a launch date of 2026-10-23, used above. Recommend confirming the plan with the delivery team before communicating a launch date externally.
+- **Security:** the stated resolution rate (95.0%) is consistent with the underlying incident counts (76/80) and required no correction.
